/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  batch26_cooling_failure  --  a BATCH exothermic reaction held at T_p by
  its jacket, and what happens when the jacket stops.

  The reaction is batch02's mass-conserving esterification,
  AcOH + EtOH -> EtOAc + H2O, first order in ethanol, with the heat of
  reaction the engine resolves from the species' standardThermochemistry
  (printed in the run log, per mol of ethanol).  The whole charge --
  equimolar acid and ethanol -- is in the vessel at t = 0.  That is what
  makes a batch the WORST case for thermal safety: at t = 0 all of the
  reactant is unconverted, so a cooling failure at the start releases the
  whole adiabatic temperature rise.

  THE SCENARIO (the recipe below):

     t < t_f   isothermal at T_p = 330 K; the jacket removes the heat of
               reaction (the energy ledger records that duty)
     t = t_f   `setParameter reactor adiabatic 1` -- the jacket stops
     t > t_f   adiabatic: the ethanol still unconverted at t_f (the
               ACCUMULATION, X_ac) reacts and heats the mass to the MTSR

  The thermal-safety estimate is MTSR = T_p + X_ac * dT_ad, with dT_ad the
  adiabatic rise of the full charge from T_p (run this case with the
  failure at t = 0 to have the engine compute it).  The engine's MTSR is
  T_final of a failure run; the EduTool puts the two side by side.

  `value 0` on the same event keeps the jacket working: the same case then
  runs the normal isothermal batch, which is how the EduTool draws X_ac(t).

  PEDAGOGICAL, NOT QUANTITATIVE (the batch02/batch06 caveat, repeated):
  the Arrhenius constants are illustrative (constant/reactions), the
  liquid heat capacities are constant (degree-0 polynomials), and the
  vessel has no vapour phase -- past the mixture's boiling point a real
  open vessel would boil and a closed one would pressurise.  The MTSR is
  defined on exactly that hypothetical, which is why it is compared with
  the boiling point (MTT) rather than trusted beyond it.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

units
(
    {
        name        reactor;
        type        batchReactor;

        operation
        {
            mode         isothermal;       // held by the jacket until the recipe takes it away
            T_setpoint   330 K;            // T_p, the process temperature
        }

        reaction    esterification_etac_exo;  // see constant/reactions
    }
);

recipe
(
    //  THE COOLING FAILURE.  `value 1`: from this instant the jacket removes
    //  no heat and the reactor is adiabatic.  `value 0`: the jacket keeps
    //  working (normal operation; nothing changes).
    {
        time        600;        // s   t_f, the moment the cooling fails
        action      setParameter;
        unit        reactor;
        key         adiabatic;
        value       1;
    }
);
